      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing a Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Monitoring as the external provider. This should provide a solid foundation for querying the metric data. I'm now focusing on how to integrate the Google Cloud Monitoring API into the Python script.\n\n\n**Defining the API**\n\nI'm now deep diving into the `query_metric_window` function's structure. I'm focusing on incorporating the `google.cloud.monitoring_v3` SDK, ensuring the function takes the `project_id`, `metric_type`, and `window_minutes` as input, and returns the queried data points over the time window. This involves defining the time range and constructing the API request.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865144301,
          "start": 1789865140765
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc46a21d001SSd9Sw05MbtCab",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc469d1c001kHWV4ekNWZLGu8",
      "session_id": "ses_f43b96366ffeo6N3fRfYkpc66S",
      "time_created": 1789865140765,
      "time_updated": 1789865144301
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "pm0szlwRPid69r00",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import monitoring_v3\nfrom google.api_core import datetime_helpers\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\ndef query_metric_window(project_id: str, metric_type: str, window_minutes: int):\n    client = monitoring_v3.MetricServiceClient()\n    project_name = f\"projects/{project_id}\"\n\n    now = datetime.utcnow()\n    interval = monitoring_v3.TimeInterval(\n        end_time=datetime_helpers.to_rfc3339(now),\n        start_time=datetime_helpers.to_rfc3339(now - timedelta(minutes=window_minutes)),\n    )\n\n    query = f\"\"\"\n        fetch gce_instance\n        | metric {metric_type}\n        | within {window_minutes}m\n        | group_by [], [value_max: max(value)]\n    \"\"\"\n\n    results = client.query_time_series(\n        request={\n            \"name\": project_name,\n            \"query\": query,\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(f\"Metric: {metric_type} (last {window_minutes} minutes)\")\n    for time_series in results:\n        for point in time_series.points:\n            print(f\"  {point.interval.end_time.isoformat()}: {point.value.double_value}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Replace with your Google Cloud Project ID and desired metric\n    # Example: \"your-project-id\", \"agent.googleapis.com/memory/used_bytes\"\n    PROJECT_ID = \"your-project-id\"  \n    METRIC_TYPE = \"agent.googleapis.com/memory/used_bytes\"\n    WINDOW_MINUTES = 5\n\n    if PROJECT_ID == \"your-project-id\":\n        print(\"Please replace 'your-project-id' with your actual Google Cloud Project ID.\")\n    else:\n        query_metric_window(PROJECT_ID, METRIC_TYPE, WINDOW_MINUTES)\n",
            "filePath": "query_metric_window.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
